and I hereby declare that Valerie Carol  Marian Vaz has been duly elected I would  now like to invite the winning candidate  Valerie about to say a few words  can I start by thanking you mr.  returning officer and everyone who has  been involved in mounting and presiding  over the casting of boats during this  election can I also thank the police for  looking after us and making sure that  democracy wins I also want to thank my  husband Paul Townsend my agent Ian  Robertson and my family and most of all  brilliant volunteers down there who have  helped me win this election they have  worked incredibly hard for the vision  that the Labor Party set out in our  manifesto I also want to pay tribute to  Paul Scheer who is the chief executive  was decided that he wants to retire I  don't know why because he's been an  amazing chief executive of Walsall  council but we wish him well and I want  to thank him for all his years of public  service I also want to pay tribute to my  colleague David Winnick he has been an  outstanding MP representing Warsaw law  he has bounced into the chamber in the  House of Commons every day and really  taken the fight to the government and  opposed things that have hurt his  Dickenson most and I'm sorry I won't be  seeing him sitting on those green  benches thank you David for all the work  that you have done  [Applause]  this result isn't a result just for me  it is a result for the vision that  Jeremy Corbyn and the labor policy set  out what we set out was a positive  vision for Britain that has been  responded to by the voters of wattle  south and I'd like to thank them most of  all for voting for that visions that the  Labour Party has put forward a vision  for young people a vision for those who  work those who are sick vulnerable and  those who are elderly we had a vision  for all stages of our lives so thank you  all once again for voting for me and  once again thank you to the brilliant  unsung heroes behind the scenes who help  so hard and work so hard to ensure the  election of a Labour MP in Walsall south  thank you  [Applause]  you
 

